# SSH Key Setup & Ansible Configuration\
\
## Problem Identified\
- Ubuntu server had empty `authorized_keys` file\
- No SSH key authentication configured\
- Ansible requires passwordless SSH keys to function\
\
## Solution Implemented\
\
### 1. Generated ED25519 SSH Key\
```bash\
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/portfolio_key -N ""\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf0 2. Deployed Public Key to Ubuntu Server\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/portfolio_key lab@172.16.39.136\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf0 3. Verified Key-Based Authentication\
ssh -i ~/.ssh/portfolio_key lab@172.16.39.136\
# Success: Logged in without password prompt\
4. Updated Ansible Inventory\
webservers:\
  hosts:\
    ubuntu-server:\
      ansible_host: 172.16.39.136\
      ansible_user: lab\
      ansible_ssh_private_key_file: ~/.ssh/portfolio_key
\f2\b \
}